                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="560" width="1120" height="30" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="gndbusl" value="&lt;b style='color:#E0E0E0;font-size:12px'&gt;COMMON GND BUS — Jetson GND + 12V PSU GND + module GND (header GND &amp; DC IN −)&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="564" width="1120" height="22" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>

                <mxCell id="steps" value="&lt;b style='font-size:13px;color:#0D47A1'&gt;Step-by-step: → dual-MOSFET module&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Buy:&lt;/b&gt; a &lt;b&gt;dual-MOSFET trigger switch driver module&lt;/b&gt; (D4184-class, DC 5–36V, 15A/400W) whose spec lists a &lt;b&gt;3.3–20V digital trigger&lt;/b&gt;. Avoid IRF520 boards (need 4–5V, won't fully turn on at 3.3V). Plus a &lt;b&gt;1N5408&lt;/b&gt; (3A) flyback diode. NOTE: the 3-pin header may be silk-screened &lt;b&gt;PWM / VCC / GND&lt;/b&gt; (or SIG/VCC/GND); the screw blocks may read &lt;b&gt;+ −&lt;/b&gt; for IN and OUT — match by function, not exact label.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;1.&lt;/b&gt; Power OFF (Jetson + 12V supply).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. REMOVE&lt;/b&gt; the IRLB8721 MOSFET, the 4.7kΩ pull-up (and any 1kΩ), and the T17 (+3.3V) wire — none are used.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. GREEN wire&lt;/b&gt; (T13 / BCM 27) → 3-pin header &lt;b&gt;SIG / PWM&lt;/b&gt; pin. (Same pin → no software change.)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4.&lt;/b&gt; 3-pin header &lt;b&gt;GND → Jetson GND&lt;/b&gt; (shared reference — REQUIRED, or SIG won't be seen). &lt;b&gt;VCC pin: leave open&lt;/b&gt; (it only powers the on-board LED).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;5.&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;+12V → DC IN +&lt;/b&gt; screw, &lt;b&gt;GND → DC IN −&lt;/b&gt; screw (power-in block).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;6.&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;OUT + → solenoid (+) RED&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;OUT − → solenoid (−) BLUE&lt;/b&gt; (the module switches the low side).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;7.&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;1N5408 flyback&lt;/b&gt; across the solenoid coil — band (cathode) to the (+) / OUT+ side.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='color:#1B5E20'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Software:&lt;/b&gt; unchanged. Keep the &lt;b&gt;libgpiod 3.3V drive&lt;/b&gt; on BCM 27 — 3.3V switches the module fully; the weak ~1.6V Jetson.GPIO would NOT. HIGH → solenoid opens. Module at 2A runs cold.&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E3F2FD;strokeColor=#1976D2;fontColor=#333;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=2;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="620" width="1120" height="320" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>
